  "schemaVersion": "desktop-contract-judges-v1",
  "about": "The events daemon's half of the desktop app's Judges section (0.27.1), beside Laya's in desktop-contract-v1.json. `calls` are the words the app's allow-list builds to read every judge kind and judge, to turn TypeSafe's hosted Jev or a local model server off at once, and the terminal line that turns one on; `vectors` are `judge kinds list` and `judges list` as the real owner answers them through the events CLI at each step of turning both kinds on and off; `disable` is what turning each off answers. The app's tests read the vectors as the events service's answers.",
